                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ectype",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f4a5826-ff4f-32ba-a6ee-372dc748f97c",
                                        "entry_id": "37cb875c-6006-3a4a-ae99-605aa2eeaaac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An impression (in wax, clay, &c.) of a seal or medal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f2befc4-cc86-42ad-929a-1f249cfc1ee1",
                                                "sense_id": "9f4a5826-ff4f-32ba-a6ee-372dc748f97c",
                                                "text": "Peireskius sent the Ectype of a Medal to Sir Robert Cotton, in which Britannia was with both a double and single N."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33244449-58fb-3e78-9a84-abf91fb95a71",
                                        "entry_id": "37cb875c-6006-3a4a-ae99-605aa2eeaaac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An object in relievo or embossed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b16e56a4-8e67-3fe2-a416-90fa2ec22d59",
                                        "entry_id": "37cb875c-6006-3a4a-ae99-605aa2eeaaac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A copy, reproduction; especially as contrasted with the original, archetype, or prototype."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48a05577-bba7-4533-baf9-e64d70d9f642",
                                                "sense_id": "b16e56a4-8e67-3fe2-a416-90fa2ec22d59",
                                                "text": "If my account is correct, both archetypes and ectypes are 'real' insofar as they are composed of ideas of sensation. But I draw a distinction that Johnson does not acknowledge, viz., a distinction between ontological and epistemic ectypes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae8e642e-2a61-4a2b-92da-50fe27d15bc1",
                                                "sense_id": "b16e56a4-8e67-3fe2-a416-90fa2ec22d59",
                                                "text": "The painting traces itself from itself by suddenly appearing in these ectypes. But the ectypes only mark the final accomplishment of this sudden appearance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41259ecd-b545-40b3-9d70-c6298355ea1c",
                                                "sense_id": "b16e56a4-8e67-3fe2-a416-90fa2ec22d59",
                                                "text": "It is likely that little attention has been paid to the archetype/ectype relationship in Kant scholarship in the English speaking world partly as a result of inconsistent translations of the German terms “Urbild” and “Nachbild” that make it difficult to even notice the relationship."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd02ac2c-c840-3975-b688-1e2821557b40",
                                        "entry_id": "37cb875c-6006-3a4a-ae99-605aa2eeaaac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An idea or impression that corresponds to external reality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
